  "_skill_md": "---\nname: tiktok\ndescription: Internal API for tiktok\nmetadata:\n  author: unbrowse\n  version: \"1.0\"\n  baseUrl: \"https://www.tiktok.com\"\n  authMethod: \"Session Token (tt-csrf-token)\"\n  endpointCount: 12\n  apiType: \"internal\"\n  category: \"social\"\n---\n\n# Tiktok API\n\n> Reverse-engineered internal API. Unofficial — may change without notice.\n\n## Documentation Index\n- `SKILL.md` (this file)\n- `references/REFERENCE.md` (detailed endpoint docs)\n- `references/ENDPOINTS.json` (machine-readable endpoint catalog)\n- `scripts/api.ts` (typed client interface)\n\n## Authentication\nSession Token (tt-csrf-token) — Authentication method detected from captured traffic.\n\n### Providing credentials\n- Prefer passing auth as request headers or cookies at call time (do not hardcode secrets into the skill).\n- If executing via an external proxy/executor, pass per-call credentials (cookies and/or headers) so they are not persisted.\n\n## Dependencies\n- Runtime capable of HTTPS requests.\n- If using `scripts/api.ts`: TypeScript toolchain (or transpile to JS).\n\n## Endpoints\n\n### Auth Flow (1)\n- `POST /v1/user/webid` — Obtain a web ID for authentication.\n\n### Data Read (4)\n- `GET /tiktok/popup/dispatch/v1` — Fetch popup content.\n- `GET /web/resource` — Retrieve a web resource.\n- `POST /tiktok/ppf/api/eligibility/v2` — Check eligibility for a program.\n- `POST /ttwid/check/` — Verify a TTWID value.\n\n### Data Write (2)\n- `POST /v1/list` — Create or modify a list.\n- `POST /web/report` — Submit a report.\n\n### Config (5)\n- `GET /api/compliance/settings/` — Retrieve compliance settings.\n- `GET /api/v1/web-cookie-privacy/config` — Get privacy configuration settings.\n- `GET /monitor_web/settings/browser-settings` — Get browser settings.\n- `POST /passport/web/store_region/` — Store user region.\n- `POST /service/2/abtest_config/` — Get A/B test configurations.\n\n## Quick Start\n\n### OpenClaw (Unbrowse) workflow\n- Authenticate in the browser first (no credentials are shipped with this skill).\n- Capture fresh auth locally: run `unbrowse_capture` on an authenticated page for this domain.\n- Execute via backend gate + client browser executor: `unbrowse_replay` with `executionMode=\"backend\"`.\n\nExample:\n```text\nunbrowse_replay { service: \"tiktok\", executionMode: \"backend\", endpoint: \"GET /tiktok/popup/dispatch/v1\" }\n```\n\nHere's a Quick Start to get you interacting with the TikTok API:\n\n```typescript\n// Example: Fetching popup content (data-read)\nasync function getPopupContent() {\n  try {\n    const popupData = await client.tiktok_popup_dispatch_v1();\n    console.log(\"Popup Content:\", popupData);\n    return popupData;\n  } catch (error) {\n    console.error(\"Error fetching popup content:\", error);\n    return null;\n  }\n}\n\ngetPopupContent();\n```\n\n```typescript\n// Example: Creating/modifying a list (data-write)\nasync function createList(listData: any) {\n  try {\n    const response = await client.v1_list({ data: listData });\n    console.log(\"List creation response:\", response);\n    return response;\n  } catch (error) {\n    console.error(\"Error creating list:\", error);\n    return null;\n  }\n}\n\nconst newListData = { name: \"My New List\", description: \"A test list\" };\ncreateList(newListData);\n```\n\n## Additional Notes\n\n**Type:** Reverse-engineered internal API (unofficial)\n**Auth:** Session Token (tt-csrf-token)\n**Base URL:** `https://www.tiktok.com`\n**Captured Auth:** 2 auth headers\n\n## About This Skill\n\nThis skill provides access to Tiktok's internal API — the hidden endpoints that power their web/mobile app.\nThese are NOT official public APIs. They were captured by observing network traffic while using the site.\n\n**Important:**\n- Auth tokens in `auth.json` may expire — re-capture if you get 401 errors\n- Internal APIs can change without notice — endpoints may break\n- Rate limits are unknown — be conservative with request frequency\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nUse this skill when you need to:\n- Access Tiktok data without official API access\n- Automate actions on www.tiktok.com (faster than browser automation)\n- Call the same endpoints the Tiktok frontend uses\n\n## Quick Start\n\n```typescript\nimport { TiktokClient } from \"./scripts/api.ts\";\n\n// Load captured auth from auth.json\nconst client = await TiktokClient.fromAuthFile(\"auth.json\");\n\n// Make requests to internal endpoints\nconst result = await client.get(\"/endpoint\");\n```\n\n## Captured Authentication\n\nThe `auth.json` file contains credentials extracted from browser traffic:\n- **Auth headers:** 2 (tt-csrf-token, tt-ticket-guard-public-key)\n- **Session cookies:** 0\n\nIf auth expires, re-run `unbrowse_login` or `unbrowse_capture` to refresh tokens.\n\n## Internal Endpoints (20)\n\n\n## Error Handling\n\n```typescript\ntry {\n  const data = await client.get(\"/resource\");\n} catch (err) {\n  if (err.message.includes(\"401\")) {\n    // Auth expired — need to re-capture\n    console.error(\"Auth expired, re-run unbrowse_login\");\n  } else {\n    console.error(\"API error:\", err.message);\n  }\n}\n```\n\nSee [REFERENCE.md](references/REFERENCE.md) for detailed endpoint documentation.\n"
